From 57f58babab6eb862c42459287d3b61a558855b4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:17:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] selftests/bpf: combine XDP socket storage and ordered
 CPUMAP

Keep an independent, small RFS policy inside selftests so the kernel
interfaces can be exercised without an external policy repository.
Observe application socket operations, read their hints from XDP and
use a stable tuple domain across misses and socket recreation.

Exercise real TCP/UDP IPv4/IPv6 CPU moves, send/recv/accept/splice and
zero-copy observations, error-queue exclusion and missing hints. Check
payload delivery after the CPUMAP handoff. Native TCP bursts must show
actual GRO aggregation and intact application data. Generic frags UDP
cases cover the page-pool skb copy's MAC-header bookkeeping.

Full policy choices and their userspace/hardware controllers remain
outside the kernel tree; these tests do not include samples sources.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
